    "chunk_text": "7.All debts and liabilities of the Society existing onthe day immediately preceding the date of commencementof this Act, shall be paid and discharged by the Corporationand all debts due to, subscription and contributions payableto the Society shall be paid to the Corporation for the purposeof this Act.\n\n(2) The Corporation shall have the power to borrow orraise money necessary for the furtherance of its objects andto create, execute, grant or issue any mortgages, bounds orobligations to secure the payment of such money.\n\n(3) All property of the Society, movable and immovableshall vest in the Corporation from the date of commencementof this Act.\n\n9.The Society shall be able and capable in law tocharge :\u2014\n\n(a)such fees as the Society may deem reasonable, foradmission to any seminar, course or examinationconducted by the Society;\n\n(b)fees for admission of persons to any class ofmembership of the Society; and\n\n(c)such subscriptions and fees, as the Society maydeem reasonable in respect of the services by theSociety.\n\nDebts due byor payable tothe Society.\n\nCorporationmay holdmovable orimmovableproperty.\n\nPowers to\n\ncharge fees\n\nand\n\nsubscriptions.\n\nPharmaceutical Society of Sri Lanka(Incorporation)6\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n10.The Society shall have the power to appoint anAdmissions and Ethical Practices Committee and to takesuch other steps as may be found necessary from time totime for the maintenance of professional standards anddiscipline among persons practicing or acting as pharmacistsin Sri Lanka.\n\n11.The seal of the Corporation may not be affixed toany instrument whatsoever except in the presence of twomembers who shall sign the documents or the Council shallfrom time to time by authorized standing orders and suchsigning shall be independent of the signing of any person asa witness."
