    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of March 27, 2015\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 30. 03. 2015)\n\nVALUE ADDED TAX (AMENDMENT)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 2002\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Finance\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 16.00Postage : Rs. 20.00\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 2 of the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d), and the legal effect of the section asamended is to introduce the reduction of the rate to 11% and to restrict the deferment bya Strategic Development Project under SVAT only during the project implementationperiod.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 3 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section is to extend the liability on wholesale and retail trade where the total turnoverfor a period of 3 months exceeds Rs.100 million.\n\nClause 4 : This clause amends section 5 of the principal enactment to provide for theremoval of the condition referred to in the consideration on termination of the lease.\n\nClause 5 : This clause amends section 7 of the principal enactment to extend theregistration of buying office under SVAT Scheme.\n\nClause 6 : This clause amends section 8 of the principal enactment in order to removethe deemed tax liability on locally produced fresh milk.\n\nClause 7 : This clause amends section 10 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to extend the liable threshold for registration.\n\nClause 8 : This clause amends section 16 of the principal enactment to provide for thepublication in the official website of the Inland Revenue, the inactive files which may beupdated on monthly basis.\n\nClause 9 : This clause amends section 17 of the principal enactment which isconsequential to the amendment made by clause 16 of the Act."
