    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of August 01, 2014\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 04.08.2014)\n\nURBAN COUNCILS (AMENDMENT)\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Local Government andProvincial Councils\n\nto amend the Urban Councils Ordinance (Chapter 255)\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 3.00Postage : Rs. 5.00\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause repeals the proviso to section 178A of the Urban CouncilsOrdinance (Chapter 255) and the legal effect due to such repeal will be to revert back tothe procedure followed by the Urban Council when re-submitting a budget orsupplementary budget to the Council for further consideration.\n\n1Urban Councils (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 03/2014.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE URBAN COUNCILS ORDINANCE(CHAPTER 255)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Urban Councils(Amendment) Act, No. of 2014 and shall come intooperation on such date as the Minister may appoint by OrderPublished in the Gazette.\n\n2.Section 178A of the Urban Councils Ordinance(Chapter 255) as amended by the Local Authorities (SpecialProvisions) Act, No. 21 of 2012 is hereby further amendedby the repeal of the Proviso to that section.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort titleand date ofoperation.\n\nAmendmentof section178A of theUrbanCouncilsOrdinance(Chapter255).\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency.\n\nUrban Councils (Amendment)2\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs. 885 (Local), Rs. 1,180(Foreign), Payable to the SUPERINTENDENT, GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, DEPARTMENT OFGOVERNMENT INFORMATION, NO. 163, KIRULAPONA MAWATHA, POLHENGODA, COLOMBO 05 before 15thDecember each year in respect of the year following."
